{
  "_comment": "Corrections applied to free-exercise-db rows at build time, in three kinds. `patches` re-tag a row: the dataset marks every cardio machine as the generic 'machine', which cannot drive the gym equipment checklist - a user who has a rower but no treadmill is indistinguishable - so these assign the six cardio equipment values and the logging type. `superseded` drop a row that a better one already covers, naming its replacement: upstream ships a separate weighted twin for movements this app records with an optional added weight, and two rows for one movement split a lifter's history in half. Row IDs are from the upstream dataset and are stable. `renamed` give a row the plain name programs use instead of the dataset's (ADR 0013): the id stays, so history is untouched, and the old name ships as shorthand for search and as a former name an import still matches exactly.",
  "patches": {
    "Bicycling": {
      "equipment": "outdoor",
      "loggingType": "distance_time"
    },
